# Evidence bytes are load-bearing in this repository: MANIFEST.sha256, the
# provenance.json files and verify_paper_claims.py all re-derive sha256 over file
# *content*. With core.autocrlf=true and no attributes, a fresh Windows checkout
# rewrites LF to CRLF and every one of those hashes silently stops matching, while
# the files still look identical in an editor. -text pins the bytes as committed.
results/** -text
.tmp/** -text
# paper/BUILD_PIN.json records sha256 over paper.tex, paper.pdf, the figure and
# the extracted text render, so those four are evidence bytes too. The PDFs git
# already treats as binary; paper.tex and paper_text.txt it does not, and on a
# fresh core.autocrlf=true clone both come out CRLF while this working tree has
# them LF -- measured, and it is the reason the pin would have hashed to
# different values here and on a reviewer's machine.
paper/** -text
